# Pixel Bop: Blip's pixel display font. Capitals only: lower-case letters use the capitals.
#
# One block per character. The header is '@ <char>' (or '@ U+XXXX' for spaces and marks that are hard to type),
# optionally followed by 'top=N': how many pixels above the baseline the first row starts (default 7, the cap
# height). Rows below the baseline are descenders. 'X' is a pixel, '.' is empty. Width is the row length; every
# letter is followed by one empty column. Every vertical stroke is two pixels wide, so it reads across a room.
# Digits are all six wide (tabular), so a clock never shifts.

